                                </handler>
                        </handlers>
                </command><command>
                        <name>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.MasterData.PIEquipment_MS.MSModel.Commands.CreateProcessAdditionalPropertiesConfiguration</name>
                        <shortname>CreateProcessAdditionalPropertiesConfiguration</shortname>
                        <description>Creates extended process properties for the given Equipment Configuration if none exists. Each property will affect the behavior of the piece of Equipment respective to this Equipment Configuration. List of properties:     - MinQuantity: The smallest quantity the piece of Equipment can handle.    - MinLevel: The smallest quantity which is recommended for the piece of Equipment.    - Quantity: The quantity that is stored in the piece of Equipment.    - MaxLevel: The biggest quantity recommended for the piece of Equipment.    - MaxQuantity: The biggest quantity the piece of Equipment can handle.    - IsSingleLot: A flag that indicates if the piece of Equipment should only handle a Material issued from a single lot.    - IsSingleMaterial: A flag that indicates if the piece of Equipment should only handle one kind of Material.    - AllocationStateMachineNId: The identifier of the State Machine on which the system will rely on, in order to manage the allocation state of the piece of Equipment.     - AllowedMaterialGroupNId: The Material Group allowed to be used with the piece of Equipment.    - AllowedMaterialNId: The Material allowed to be used with the piece of Equipment.  The command performs a check on the Equipment Configuration Id to see if it exists. If not, error 11214 is returned.</description>
                        <assembly>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.MasterData.PIEquipment_MS.MSModel.Commands, Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null</assembly>
                        <dotnetcommandtype></dotnetcommandtype>
                        <commandtype>Undefined</commandtype>
                        <domain>MasterData</domain>
                        <visibility>Protected</visibility>
                        <composite>false</composite>
                        <taglist>
                        </taglist>
                        <securable>true</securable>
                        <handlers>
                                <handler>
                                        <name>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.MasterData.PIEquipment_MS.MSModel.Commands.CreateProcessAdditionalPropertiesConfigurationHandlerShell</name>
                                        <assembly>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.PIEquipment_MS.CommandHandler, Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null</assembly>
                                        <target_cpu>AnyCPU</target_cpu>
                                        <targetframework>netstandard2.0</targetframework>
                                        <dependencies></dependencies>
                                </handler>
                        </handlers>
                </command><command>
